   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fgQ",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'm standing to finish the job on RMA reform: stronger property rights, less council interference, and more homes and investment. I'll hold the Government and councils to those commitments as plans and rules are written, so ACT's wins deliver real benefits for communities. Growth must have infrastructure funding and financing agreed, so roads, water and wastewater keep pace. Give your party vote to ACT to help me deliver these reforms and unlock New Zealand's potential."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fiL",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I bring 23 years' experience as a civil and environmental engineer and six years as an ACT MP. As Parliamentary Under-Secretary, I've helped secure stronger property rights in RMA reform and led national policy direction recognising infrastructure's importance. I'll work to prevent those gains being diluted during implementation. I've also developed ACT's transport, electricity, energy and resources policies to get traffic moving, grow the grid and unlock reliable, affordable domestic energy, supporting jobs and investment."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fkG",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Deliver ACT's RMA reforms: stronger property rights, fewer consents and lower costs."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fmB",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Secure infrastructure funding, financing and delivery dates before new development proceeds."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fo6",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Unlock NZ's gas and mineral resources to deliver reliable energy, lower costs and more jobs."
     }
    ],
