   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6frw",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I am running for Parliament because I believe Aotearoa can be fairer, cleaner, and more compassionate. I believe climate policies are cost of living policies. I want a future where everyone has a warm home, a well-paid job, strong public services, with a safe and flourishing environment. The Greens put people and planet first, making decisions for future generations, and ensuring every community has a real voice, and costs are borne fairly."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6ftr",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I was born and raised in West Auckland and have lived in Ti Point (near Leigh) for 13 years. I commute an hour and a half to Auckland for work during the week and see the changes to the electorate on a daily basis. There has been a large amount of development in all areas, fast-tracking the strain on infrastructure, traffic and the environment, while running roughshod over local voices."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fvm",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Reforming the tax system to reduce the cost of living pressure for 96% of Kiwi families."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fxh",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Ending fast-track development to protect nature, uphold Te Tiriti, and give communities a real say."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6fzc",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Protecting our rivers & harbours so everyone can drink, swim, and fish in clean, healthy waterways. "
     }
    ],
